# A reverse mDNS reply, in the shape a responder really sends one: an answer
# for the address asked about, plus a record it volunteers alongside.
#
# flags 0x8400 = response + authoritative: in mDNS every responder is
# authoritative, because it only ever answers for itself.
#
#   answer     42.1.168.192.in-addr.arpa.     PTR ttl 10  laptop.local.
#   additional laptop._device-info._tcp.local TXT ttl 10  model=Example1,1
#
# The additional record is volunteered, not asked for: responders add what
# they think the querier will want next. Both names are compressed - 0xc00c
# is "the name at offset 12", and the TXT owner points back into the answer's
# rdata for its ".local" suffix.
